# Code ownership → review routing. GitHub requests review from the owner automatically on any PR that
# touches a matching path. This is a small, single-maintainer project, so the default owner is the
# maintainer; the point of the specific rules below is to make the SAFETY-CRITICAL and CONTRACT paths
# impossible to change without that being visible in the review, not to distribute ownership.

# Default owner for everything.
*                                   @zgranowitz

# The cross-app contract. On narrow `main` a change here ripples to Garmin (Venu 3S) and the widgets, and
# to the faBolusGarmin repo's Monkey C mirror — the schema-drift checks enforce the mirror, but the
# semantics are a human-review concern. The Apple Watch remote and the Mac menu-bar remote are
# EXPERIMENTAL-ONLY (v0.5.0 narrow-main; preserved on `dev/watch-remote` / `dev/mac`, not on `main`) — a
# schema change there is a `dev/*`/`experimental` concern, not a `main` one.
/schema/                            @zgranowitz

